A build trace whose output is no longer valid reads as no realisation.

Garbage collection deletes a content-addressed output but keeps its row in
BuildTraceV3. A lookup that returned such a row made the build take the
missing path for the built output: DerivationGoal::checkPathValidity found
the trace, the path was absent, and assertPathValidity failed with
"some outputs are unexpectedly invalid" -- every build needing that output,
until the row was deleted by hand (a day of failed galaxybook builds,
2026-11-04; victus-15's GC once left 8640 such rows). queryRealisationUncached,
which every realisation query goes through (builds, the daemon's clients,
harmonia), now answers "unbuilt" for a stale row, so the output is rebuilt
or substituted, and nix-ca-rebuild-after-gc.patch's registerDrvOutput then
replaces the row. Applies on top of that patch.

--- a/src/libstore/local-store.cc	2026-11-19 22:53:06.578319358 +0900
+++ b/src/libstore/local-store.cc	2026-11-19 22:53:14.889236505 +0900
@@ -1651,8 +1651,21 @@
     const DrvOutput & id, Callback<std::shared_ptr<const UnkeyedRealisation>> callback) noexcept
 {
     try {
-        auto maybeRealisation = retrySQLite<std::optional<const UnkeyedRealisation>>(
-            [&]() { return queryRealisation_(*_state->lock(), id); });
+        auto maybeRealisation =
+            retrySQLite<std::optional<const UnkeyedRealisation>>([&]() -> std::optional<const UnkeyedRealisation> {
+                auto state(_state->lock());
+                auto r = queryRealisation_(*state, id);
+                /* A build trace whose output is no longer valid (garbage
+                   collection deletes outputs, not their traces) is not a
+                   realisation: answering with it makes the caller take a
+                   missing path for the built output ("some outputs are
+                   unexpectedly invalid"). Report the output as unbuilt, so
+                   it is rebuilt or substituted; registerDrvOutput then
+                   replaces the stale row. */
+                if (r && !isValidPath_(*state, r->outPath))
+                    return std::nullopt;
+                return r;
+            });
         if (maybeRealisation)
             callback(std::make_shared<const UnkeyedRealisation>(maybeRealisation.value()));
         else
